@* Status timeline of a yes/no check (service, process, pending restart, file, antivirus and firewall) or a script check: one block per
   bucket, teal when every result was fine, red when at least one was a problem, amber when the check could not run, gray without results.
   With BlockSelected (script checks, 0.9.0) a block with results can be clicked to list its runs. *@
@inject TimeDisplay Time

<div class="status-timeline" role="img" aria-label="@($"Status history of {View.Name}")">
    @foreach (var point in View.Points)
    {
        @if (BlockSelected.HasDelegate && point.HasData)
        {
            <span class="status-timeline-block selectable @CssClass(point) @(point.Time == Selected ? "selected" : "")"
                  title="@($"{Tooltip(point)}. Click to see its runs and their output.")" role="button" tabindex="0"
                  @onclick="@(() => BlockSelected.InvokeAsync(point))" @onkeydown="@(e => OnKeyAsync(e, point))"></span>
        }
        else
        {
            <span class="status-timeline-block @CssClass(point)" title="@Tooltip(point)"></span>
        }
    }
</div>
<div class="d-flex justify-space-between muted mt-1" style="font-size:0.75rem">
    <span>@Time.Absolute(View.From)</span>
    <span>@Time.Absolute(View.To)</span>
</div>
<div class="d-flex gap-3 mt-2 muted flex-wrap" style="font-size:0.75rem">
    <span><span class="status-timeline-block status-timeline-ok legend"></span> @FineText</span>
    <span><span class="status-timeline-block status-timeline-problem legend"></span> @ProblemText</span>
    <span><span class="status-timeline-block status-timeline-error legend"></span> Could not run</span>
    <span><span class="status-timeline-block status-timeline-empty legend"></span> No results</span>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public CheckHistoryView View { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>Called when a block with results is clicked; without it the blocks cannot be clicked.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<HistoryPoint> BlockSelected { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The start of the selected block, which is outlined.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public DateTime? Selected { get; set; }

    private Task OnKeyAsync(KeyboardEventArgs e, HistoryPoint point) =>
        e.Key is "Enter" or " " ? BlockSelected.InvokeAsync(point) : Task.CompletedTask;

    private bool ExitCode => View.Kind == ThresholdKind.ExitCode;

    private string FineText => ExitCode ? "Exit code that is OK" : Ui.CheckValue(View.Type, 1, View.Target, View.Parameters);

    private string ProblemText => ExitCode ? "Exit code that is a warning or an error" : Ui.CheckValue(View.Type, 0, View.Target, View.Parameters);

    /// <summary>
    /// A script check (0.9.0) is judged with the exit codes of its script when the history knows them (<see cref="HistoryPoint.HasProblem"/>).
    /// Otherwise flag values are 1 (fine) and 0 (problem), so the minimum of a bucket tells whether a problem occurred, and a script
    /// bucket from before 0.9.0 is fine only with exit code 0.
    /// </summary>
    private bool IsProblem(HistoryPoint point) =>
        point.HasProblem ?? (ExitCode ? point.Min is { } min && (min != 0 || point.Max != 0) : point.Min is < 1);

    private string CssClass(HistoryPoint point) =>
        IsProblem(point) ? "status-timeline-problem"
        : point.Values > 0 ? "status-timeline-ok"
        : point.Errors + point.NoResponses > 0 ? "status-timeline-error"
        : "status-timeline-empty";

    private string Tooltip(HistoryPoint point)
    {
        var when = Time.Absolute(point.Time);
        if (!point.HasData)
        {
            return $"{when}: no results";
        }

        var text = IsProblem(point) ? ProblemText : point.Values > 0 ? FineText : "Could not run";
        return point.Errors > 0 && point.Values > 0 ? $"{when}: {text}, {point.Errors} could not run" : $"{when}: {text}";
    }
}
